DynamoDB, Amazon.com lowered workflow-execution overhead by 90 percent, decommissioned hundreds of Oracle hosts, and reduced time needed to scale for large events by 90 percent. Amazon\u0027s internal workflow-orchestration engine—known as Herd—powers the business logic for processing worldwide Amazon.com customer orders.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/case-studies/US/amazon_logo_RGB.f7a9122003537a33696a46bbf1ad1c874bfb38c0.jpg","displayLocation":"Americas","footerInfoText":"Published Date","description":"\u003cp\u003eUsing Amazon DynamoDB, Amazon.com lowered workflow-execution overhead by 90 percent, decommissioned hundreds of Oracle hosts, and reduced time needed to scale for large events by 90 percent. Amazon\u0019s internal workflow-orchestration engine\u0014known as Herd\u0014powers the business logic for processing worldwide Amazon.com customer orders. The Amazon Herd team moved its system from Oracle to Amazon DynamoDB.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","industry":"Retail","sortDate":"2017-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/herd/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"Herd","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2017","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"Herd Case Study"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#use-case#general-database-migration","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#use-case","name":"General Database Migration","description":"General Database Migration","dateCreated":"2020-06-05T06:37:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:41+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#category#database-migration","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"Database Migration","description":"Database Migration","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:31:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-12T02:01:30+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#language","name":"English","description":"English","dateCreated":"2020-03-03T06:40:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:23+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#category#batch-processing","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"Batch Processing","description":"Batch Processing","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:31:02+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-26T01:35:02+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Databases","description":"Databases","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:14+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:27+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#location#americas","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"Americas","description":"Americas","dateCreated":"2020-02-03T05:29:01+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:29+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#customer-story","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Customer Story","description":"Customer Story","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#industry#retail","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#industry","name":"Retail","description":"Retail","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:42:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:08+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#dynamodb","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon DynamoDB","description":"Amazon DynamoDB","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:02:48+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:31+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#customer-segment#enterprise","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#customer-segment","name":"Enterprise (ENT)","description":"Enterprise (ENT)","dateCreated":"2021-06-04T06:35:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:14+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#case-study","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Case Study","description":"Case Study","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#serverless","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Serverless","description":"Serverless","dateCreated":"2021-07-28T18:46:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:33+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#migration","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Migration","description":"Migration","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:28+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#industry#transport-logistics","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#industry","name":"Transport \u0026 Logistics","description":"Transport \u0026 Logistics","dateCreated":"2020-06-25T04:08:39+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:09+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#category#databases","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#category","name":"Databases","description":"Databases","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:31:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-12T02:01:30+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#customer-segment#enterprise","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#customer-segment","name":"Enterprise","description":"Enterprise","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T18:39:40+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-05T01:27:39+0000"},{"id":"customer-references#innovator#amazon","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"customer-references#innovator","name":"Amazon","description":"Amazon","dateCreated":"2022-04-25T19:05:23+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-06-27T20:43:38+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#zoona-case-study","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"zoona-case-study","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T19:44:05+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-07-14T23:32:38+0000","additionalFields":{"featured":"0","descriptionSummary":"Using AWS, Zoona cut IT costs in half while increasing the size of its infrastructure and the number of IT services it supports. The company, which helps people in sub-Saharan Africa gain access to financial services for the first time, has more than 1.6 million customers using Zoona to make electronic money transfers.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/Zoona_Customer-Reference_Logo.ed2c1a163afcb4d4f5c1e39f23a47d05fe29494c.png","displayLocation":"Sub-Saharan Africa","footerInfoText":"Published Date","description":"\u003cp\u003eUsing AWS, Zoona cut IT costs in half while increasing the size of its infrastructure and the number of IT services it supports. The company, which helps people in sub-Saharan Africa gain access to financial services for the first time, has more than 1.6 million customers using Zoona to make electronic money transfers. Zoona built a microservices architecture on AWS with Amazon EC2 instances supporting all applications, Amazon RDS supporting MySQL and PostgreSQL databases, and Amazon DynamoDB running Datomic, a distributed database.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","industry":"Financial Services","sortDate":"2017-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/zoona/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"Zoona","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2017","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"Zoona Case Study"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#language","name":"English","description":"English","dateCreated":"2020-03-03T06:40:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:23+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#compute","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Compute","description":"Compute","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:11+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:23+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#location#middle-east-africa","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"Middle East \u0026 Africa","description":"Middle East \u0026 Africa","dateCreated":"2020-02-03T05:30:19+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:53+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#location#africa","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"Africa","description":"Africa","dateCreated":"2020-04-09T03:54:59+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:56+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#industry#financial-services","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#industry","name":"Financial Services","description