e \u0026 Internet","dateCreated":"2020-06-25T04:08:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:09+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#aws-case-study-international-centre-for-radio-astronomy-research-icrar","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"aws-case-study-international-centre-for-radio-astronomy-research-icrar","dateCreated":"2019-07-22T19:59:22+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-01-21T02:43:07+0000","additionalFields":{"featured":"0","descriptionSummary":"The International Centre for Radio Astronomy Research (ICRAR) is part of a large international team developing the Square Kilometre Array (SKA)—a universe-mapping radio telescope of unprecedented size and sensitivity. By using AWS to manage crowd-sourced CPU cycles, ICRAR has the compute capacity to analyze between 400 and 500 galaxies simultaneously.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/ICRAR_Customer-Reference_Logo.3d25f79bab0f0c31226fe12dfa04cabb5080de9e.png","displayLocation":"Asia Pacific","footerInfoText":"Published Date","description":"\u003cp\u003eThe International Centre for Radio Astronomy Research (ICRAR) is part of a large international team currently developing the Square Kilometre Array (SKA) ? a Universe-mapping radio telescope of unprecedented size and sensitivity. By using AWS to manage crowd-sourced CPU cycles, ICRAR has the compute capacity to analyze between 400 and 500 galaxies simultaneously.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n","industry":"Government","sortDate":"2014-01-01","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/icrar/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"International Centre for Radio Astronomy Research (ICRAR)","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2014","contentType":"Customer Story","headline":"AWS Case Study: International Centre for Radio Astronomy Research (ICRAR)"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#product#glacier","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon S3 Glacier","description":